
Create SSH keys
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "SECOND_EMAIL@example.com" -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_second_github

Confirm files exist
ls -al ~/.ssh | grep zbolabs

Add the new key to your SSH agent. Looks like it adds the key to apple keychain.
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_second_github


Check that it loaded:
ssh-add -l


Copy the public key and add to second github account. You add this on the GitHub settings section for SSH (https://github.com/settings/keys).
pbcopy < ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_second_github.pub

Test the key
ssh -T git@github-second